      "gap_category": "other:public_policy_ambiguity",
      "v1_status": "gap",
      "mechanism_sketch": "The join itself is now expressible (population calendly.invitees + exact lookup of scheduled_events by event_id; lookups are exact single-key, populations.py:280-301). What is not decidable is which event the report means: at 09:00Z the only event dated 'today' (Product Demo 15:00Z) has not happened; the only past active event (Discovery Call) is Feb 10; the Feb 14 call is cancelled. Resolution A ('event dated today') is expressible now as required_when start date == 2026-02-15. Resolution B ('most recent past active event') needs a selection ordered by a joined field (SelectionAlias.where/order_by read only member/request/lookups, obligations.py:62-80, and invitees carry no date), i.e. member-level lookups inside selections (cross_system_reconciliation), plus timestamp ordering (values.py:229-231 collapses iso_timestamp to a UTC date). Needs a coordinator decision first; neither reading is invented here.",
      "reused_by": [
        "operations.calendly_equipment_inspection",
        "finance.payment_reconciliation"
      ],
      "note": "Calendly 'cancelled' vs schema literal 'canceled' only matters for typed projections; obligation populations read raw strings.",
      "v2_status": "gap",
      "v3_note": "Still a policy decision. Mechanism 6 now makes reading A decidable (iso_instant start within the bound 2026-02-15 day, and 'already started' versus the 10:00Z clock); reading B (most recent past active event of the invitee) still needs member-level lookups inside selections (invitee->event join per member; SelectionAlias.where reads member/request/lookups only).",
      "v3_status": "gap"
    },
