      "kind": "report",
      "status": "expressed",
      "v1_status": "gap",
      "mechanism_sketch": "mentions has words/verbatim/amount modes only (predicates.py:140-171); a scheduled time can be written as '2026-02-10 14:00 UTC', 'Feb 10, 2:00 PM UTC' or '9:00 AM ET'. Needs mentions mode 'datetime' with a typed instant (iso_timestamp input that keeps the time and offset), declared accepted renderings and timezone conversion, unknown on unlabelled local times. With it, effect_match can couple subject and time per accepted event (any(all(subject==A, time A), all(subject==B, time B))). Luna wrote '2026-02-10 14:00-14:30 America/New_York' for a 14:00Z event, which such a check should score 0.",
      "reused_by": [
        "operations.calendly_equipment_inspection",
        "operations.zoom_training_setup",
        "hr.break_schedule_processing"
      ],
      "v2_status": "gap",
      "check_id": "followup-scheduled-time",
      "note": "Mechanisms 6/7: per accepted event, subject == template AND the description gives its start as a time of day: the UTC clock time (from iso_instant(start) - iso_instant(UTC midnight), /60) on a line without a non-UTC zone label, or the America/New_York wall time (UTC-5 in February) next to an Eastern label (mentions_together). Coupling means a Discovery Call subject needs 14:00 / 2:00 PM, Product Demo 15:00. The date is not required. Luna wrote '14:00-14:30 America/New_York' for a 14:00 UTC event -> 0 (states 19:00 UTC).",
      "v3_limitation": "Zone handling is enumerated (UTC unlabelled/labelled, Eastern conversion; other US zone labels on the UTC wall time count as mislabelled). A correct conversion to another zone (e.g. '6:00 AM PT') is a false 0. Smallest mechanism: mentions mode 'instant' that reads a time with its zone label and compares UTC instants, default zone declared.",
      "v3_status": "expressed"
